Arena: tolerate an already emptied arena in destruct_contents()

move_contents() empties the arena it moves out of:

  Arena *Arena::move_contents(Arena *copy) {
    copy->destruct_contents();
    copy->_first = _first;
    ...
    reset();                      // _first = _chunk = _hwm = NULL
    return copy;
  }

Matcher::match() calls it as

  C->node_arena()->move_contents(C->old_arena());

so node_arena is left reset with _first == NULL.  Compile::~Compile() then
destroys node_arena, Arena::~Arena() calls destruct_contents(), and

  _first->chop();

dereferences NULL.  destruct_contents() already tests _first for the
UseMallocOnly path, so a NULL _first is an expected state here; the chop
simply lacks the same guard.

On the android server build this aborted VM startup every time: the first
runtime stub (OptoRuntime::generate_stub, _new_instance_Java) runs the
matcher, and the C2 compiler thread then died in

  Arena::destruct_contents() <- Arena::~Arena() <- Compile::~Compile()

with fault addr 0x0.  -Xint never runs the compiler, which is why it worked.

Chop only when there is something to chop.  reset() still runs, so the
empty arena keeps its invariants.

diff --git a/hotspot/src/share/vm/memory/allocation.cpp b/hotspot/src/share/vm/memory/allocation.cpp
index 3cd30a6..9bae580 100644
--- a/hotspot/src/share/vm/memory/allocation.cpp
+++ b/hotspot/src/share/vm/memory/allocation.cpp
@@ -521,7 +521,11 @@ void Arena::destruct_contents() {
   // reset size before chop to avoid a rare racing condition
   // that can have total arena memory exceed total chunk memory
   set_size_in_bytes(0);
-  _first->chop();
+  // move_contents() resets the arena it moves out of, so by the time the
+  // destructor runs _first can already be NULL; only chop what is left.
+  if (_first != NULL) {
+    _first->chop();
+  }
   reset();
 }
 
